WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:17.870
Lingalind, a world surrounded by a wall.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:23.040
The wall enshrouds the land,
protecting, nurturing, sustaining.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:29.620
The wall is god. That is the basis of Lingalind.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:36.490
On that fated day, a man fell from the sky
on the remote village of Edger in Iki.

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:42.490
This man of missing memories
controlled a Briheight without conviction.

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:47.370
He said, "I'm going back beyond the wall."

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:52.200
To Lingalind, he defies common sense. His name:

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.160
Arrow. Back Arrow.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.080
Come on, tell us your real name!

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:01.620
You can't just... Hey!
Listen when people are talking!

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.620
Um... Could you wear them, please?

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:10.120
Sure... This memento of your dad
is in safe hands with me!

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.410
I owe you one! Thanks!

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:13.910
Manifest Armor...

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:20.160
See you guys! Later!

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:21.410
Where are you going?!

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:27.450
Beyond the wall! I hate to leave,
but I've gotta go back! Take care!

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:28.660
Ren, let's go!

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.490
Right!

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.240
What's his deal?

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.040
Atlee!

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:13.790
Is Having Dreams a Burden?

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:17.090
Is Having Dreams a Burden?

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.290
I keep going and going
but it's not getting closer!

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:36.490
I'm starving! Can't some food fall from the sky?

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:37.870
My goodness.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.240
The wall's bigger than it looks.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:45.410
It seems close, but it could take
months to get there.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.330
Who are you guys?

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.370
My name's Shu Bi.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:53.450
Fascinating. You were
in that for five-plus hours?

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:55.830
Your conviction's something else.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.240
You think so?

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.870
Most people struggle with one or two.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.990
It's just my second time, so I wouldn't know.

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:04.370
Second time?

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:07.490
Did you really come from beyond the wall?

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:07.890
Yeah.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.660
What's out there?

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.990
Don't know. But I will once I go back beyond--

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:16.910
There's no "beyond the wall"! There just isn't!

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:19.870
That sort of reaction is normal.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:23.620
The wall enshrouds the land,
nurturing and protecting.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:25.330
Beyond, there's nothing.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:31.540
Our entire world, Lingalind,
is within the walls... or so people believe.

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:32.830
And you?

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:35.200
Well, I'm a genius!

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.540
What's your point?

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.830
The wall's at least 10,000 gents.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:42.740
Ten-thousand gents?

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:48.540
I'm 1.78 gents tall.
It's roughly 5,678 times that.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:54.490
Think you can scale over 5,678 mes stacked high?

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.620
You damn brute!

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:02.620
Ren! Stop-- Oof!

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.620
How dare you strike Sir Shu!

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.410
He kinda pissed me off, but now I know:

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:15.410
I can send one of him flying,
but not 5,687 hims.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.410
Stop blabbering nonsense!

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.700
That's enough, Ren!

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:25.330
Arrow, you have a very unique
style of communication.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:28.370
I bet you're hungry. Help yourself.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.950
Thanks.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.120
Mmm! Yummy!

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:37.620
Of course. It's ant-eating boar thigh.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:41.830
And Ren here is surprisingly good at cooking.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:44.740
You can't stop me from going to the wall.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.200
I won't stop you.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.540
S-Sir Shu?

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:49.910
You'll help me then? Great!

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:53.790
In exchange, I'd like you to wait several days.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.200
Huh?

00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:00.490
The stars border the heavens and
the towering wall is the edge of the world.

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:05.290
Even I don't know enough
to challenge that logic just yet.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.870
Is there any reason to trust you?

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:10.700
Is there any reason to doubt me?

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:16.200
No to both, 'cuz I can't remember anything.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:22.200
I'm glad you're a man of reason,
but I'm asking since it works for me.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:25.160
Only trust me if it works for you.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:28.240
I wouldn't like 5,678 of you,

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:32.410
but the way you talk
makes me think I can trust you.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:40.120
Her conviction and emotional levels
seem to be back to normal.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.740
Um, I...

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:45.040
Just rest a little longer. You're tired.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:45.910
But--!

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:49.950
Briheights manifest by the power of one's will.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:53.540
You're hardy to wake so soon
after your first time.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:56.790
We're tough cookies here in Edger Village!

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:58.410
Why is Bit bragging?

00:06:58.410 --> 00:06:59.410
That guy--!

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.200
Mr. Panties ran off.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:05.410
We've gotta find him!
Even in a Briheight, he'll never make it!

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:08.200
He wrecked my house! Forget him!

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:10.830
Even so, he saved me!

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:13.990
What?!

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.950
Looks like he's sleeping.

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:23.620
What'd he come back for?

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:26.490
A scary-looking lady dropped him off.

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:28.910
It's not like he belongs here!

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:33.290
Sir Shu, what exactly are you planning?

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:35.040
Will you stop me if I--

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:37.330
I wouldn't waste my time.

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:43.580
But don't utter "beyond the wall"
in the imperial court.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:46.990
If His Majesty hears word of it,
even you won't--

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:49.160
Won't be spared?

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.790
Yeah, I know better than that.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:58.200
Finally decide to come back, Shu?

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:03.660
Oh? Sneaking back after
a late-night rendezvous, are we?

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:05.830
What happened to your face?

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:13.160
Did you make a move on Ren
and get smacked? Probably deserved it.

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:14.080
That's not--

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:19.290
Relax, Ren Sin. I know this guy
doesn't have it in him.

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:21.240
You're so rude, Kai.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:26.740
But here I am, waiting for you.
Did you find the second Rakuho?

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:27.870
Shu?

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:31.580
Wait a day and I'll give a report.

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:36.330
Be careful. I don't wanna see
my childhood buddy end up bloody.

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:40.120
Don't worry, I'm famously thick-skinned!

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:52.840
Arrow! Play chopscotch!

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:53.450
Huh?

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:56.790
You're the chopper! Split this with your head!

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:57.790
Okay!

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:02.620
Whoa!

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:05.190
Okay! Now it's my turn to throw!

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:05.830
Huh?!

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:08.160
Ready?! Here it comes!

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:12.290
Cut it out, guys. I'm sure Arrow is still tired.

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:14.790
Run! It's the sheriff!

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:19.160
I'm sorry the kids were bothering you.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:22.950
Nah. I know I've got a hard head thanks to them.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:24.540
Huh? You're bleeding!

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.540
Huh?

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:33.040
Thanks. And for the clothes, too.

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:34.840
Thank Bit for that.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:35.370
Hmm?

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:40.240
He sewed it with scraps.
Bit's the best tailor in town.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:42.580
Sucks at shooting though.

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:43.220
Shuddap.

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:44.330
Really?

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:45.910
Got a problem with 'em?!

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:47.830
Nah, it's well made!

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:49.900
Yeah?

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:51.120
I like it!

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:56.450
Well I don't like you, but you did
save Atlee. This makes us even!

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.160
I never owed you.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.990
You wrecked my house!

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:02.950
Oh yeah! Sorry about that!

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:04.790
Okay, I'll rebuild it!

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.790
That should do it!

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:10.410
What is this even?! A house?!

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:14.080
I'll add a roof and walls
once I find more stuff.

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:16.330
You're staying here then?

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:17.950
Huh?

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:24.490
Didn't you run away from your homeland
using a Rakuho or something?

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:28.370
But you lost control, hit your head,
and lost your memories.

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:30.990
Right? Or is this all an act?

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:34.870
Yeah! That's what I always thought! Well?!

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:38.950
I came from beyond the wall.
That much is certain.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.040
Come on.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:47.870
Elsha?

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:51.290
Atlee, stay behind. Come on.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:52.490
What?

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:59.290
In just four shots! That's Elsha for you!

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:00.490
Looks tasty!

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:04.870
Look. That's our Edger Village right there.

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:11.580
We hunt for food and grow a handful
of vegetables. We're barely just surviving.

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:16.080
That's the kind of place we live in.
See how small it is?

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:18.910
Wouldn't know. Haven't been anywhere else.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:24.080
The kids that Atlee looks after
don't have any parents.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:29.410
Epidemics, hunting accidents...
Lots of things kill people here.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:35.370
Atlee, Bit, and I lost our parents, too.
We can't afford additional risk.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:36.790
Meaning me?

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:39.450
Thugs will hunt the Rakuho down.

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:42.870
You all seem spunky to me, though.

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:47.450
We live to the fullest because
tomorrow might not come.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:50.080
Can't you just go somewhere else?

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:55.290
To where?! For your information,
Rekka and Lutoh are in a huge war!

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:59.700
Our ancestors got pushed out
of their lands and came here!

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:06.240
They had to beg Iki for permission
to live here and barely scrape by!

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:10.410
There's always outside. Just go beyond the wall.

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:14.910
I'm telling you, it doesn't exist.

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:21.080
And we can't support a stranger,
let alone follow impossible dreams.

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:26.580
You can take the hornhare,
but I'm afraid you can't stay.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:30.370
And these, too. Water and dried deerhorse.

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:32.950
This is the most we can do for you.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:45.070
Republic of Rekka

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:45.830
While you keep an eye on
Edger Village, I'll stay here and--

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:48.450
What are you doing that's dangerous?!

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:50.540
Imperial Library

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:52.700
I knew I couldn't hide it from you. Look.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:55.950
The seal to enter the banned texts archive?

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:59.290
Only His Majesty and
the prime minister have one.

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:01.410
I knew such a time would come.

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:03.080
Did you make a copy of--?!

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:05.540
You're too loud. We're short on time.

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:10.330
I have a lot to figure out before
the world reacts to our Rakuho man.

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:10.890
Huh?

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:13.330
The bandit who attacked Edger Village

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:15.740
likely worked for Lutoh.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:20.950
Supremacy of Lutoh - Maestrog Castle

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:20.950
Your Bind Warper?

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:22.410
Yes.

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:24.490
Indeed, it's broken.

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.580
A man was in the Rakuho?

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:31.450
And when you lost the battle,
you lived and only your Bind Warper broke?

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:34.080
It goes against everything we know.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:42.580
I overheard your conversation.
Is this not tremendous news?

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:45.790
No. You need not concern yourself, Princess.

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:47.990
Princess... Fine Forté?

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:50.410
Begone. Your presence is insulting to--

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:52.080
No, I don't mind.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:56.910
Are you the one I've heard
has been working for our Lutoh?

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:58.370
Y-Yes.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:00.370
Princess, you shouldn't.

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:02.200
He's lowborn. You're wasting--

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:04.450
I don't mind. Raise your head.

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:05.790
Of course.

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:12.160
People like you are helpful when
our military can't act publicly. Thank you.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:14.700
No, I don't deserve it.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:18.410
Why is it that people must kill each other?

00:14:18.410 --> 00:14:19.410
Huh?

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:24.120
It's sad. If no one has to die
when we fight with Briheights,

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:29.870
I'd like to know how the Rakuho man
does it. I wish I could meet him.

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:31.120
Princess...

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:36.290
But if we marched our troops there,
Rekka would throw a fit.

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:42.990
I know. But that man could be the key
which leads to world peace.

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:48.490
I, Peath Glinhouse, fully understand
your peace-loving heart.

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:49.450
You mean...?

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.040
Yes.

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:55.290
Iki Territory       Presidential Estate

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:55.290
It's that simple.
Isn't Edger Village your territory?

00:14:55.290 --> 00:15:00.950
Wish I could help you, Secretary Peath,
but we're an independent nation.

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:04.160
We may be weak, but bossing us around isn't--

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:05.950
President Garay...

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:11.830
Unlike the princess,
many of us here are itching for battle.

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:15.700
I see your point. What exactly do you want?

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.410
What's with all this meat?

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:22.540
I wonder if it's Arrow's doing?

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:25.540
He's sure hung up on paying debts.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:32.490
Attention, Edger Village!
We're Iki Territory's Self-Defense Force!

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.950
The military? You're kidding!

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:39.580
I, Commander Tyrone Duster,

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.080
hereby order the village to be searched!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:42.750
Do it!

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:43.740
Yes, sir!

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:46.240
Huh?! What's going on?!

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:48.120
I-I'm sorry!

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:54.950
Don't panic! If you do as I say,
no one gets hurt!

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.620
I've always wanted to say that!

00:15:57.620 --> 00:15:59.950
What's the point of this search?

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:06.620
Are you the chief? Hand over the man
who landed in the Rakuho here!

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:10.740
If you're looking for him, he left!

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.080
Say what?!

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:14.950
You get all that, Mr. President?

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:17.700
Enough. Make it disappear.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:23.290
We don't want Rekka showing up, too.
Erase Edger Village from the map.

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:24.200
Huh?!

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:26.290
Yes, sir!

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:27.160
Manifest Armor...

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:32.120
All troops, prepare for battle!
Burn the village! Slaughter 'em all!

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:35.700
Got it?! This is not a drill!

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:40.620
I've always wanted to say that!

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:44.450
This is not a drill! It's the real deal!

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:48.740
Not my house again!

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:52.660
Stop it! Arrow isn't here anymore! He left!

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:52.660
Manifest Armor...

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:54.370
Atlee! Not again!

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:57.120
So stop harassing our village!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:01.910
You brought out a Briheight?
Sounds like you're resisting!

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:03.790
I'll destroy the village!

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:09.290
It's up to me to make a small sacrifice
for the greater good!

00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:12.830
I've always wanted to say that, too!

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:15.580
A small sacrifice for the greater--

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:18.540
That's a terrible thing to say!

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:25.240
Bad news for you, lady!

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:27.240
My conviction is...

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:31.200
Don't get roped into things!

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:41.330
Argh, dangit! Where's another Warper?!

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:47.160
Why is everyone we fight a maniac?!

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:51.040
Found one! Found one!
Found one! I really found one!

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:54.450
There was another Bind Warper in the Rakuho!

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:55.790
Here goes!

00:17:56.870 --> 00:17:58.580
--Manifest Armor...
--Elsha!

00:17:58.580 --> 00:17:59.990
What?!

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:03.450
There's two Briheights in <i>this</i> place?!

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:09.040
I'm the one who made Arrow leave,
so I've gotta step up!

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:13.370
Holy hell! Elsha made a Briheight, too!

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:19.660
Let Atlee go! If you don't--

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:21.410
Huh?!

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:22.490
Huh?

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:30.580
Elsha! You alive?! Hey!

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:36.040
That was anticlimactic!
But to think you had two Briheights!

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:41.870
Mr. President was right! A village
this dangerous should be wiped out!

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:51.200
Take off the Bind Warper, Atlee!

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:52.290
Right!

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:59.580
This can't be! It's all because of that man!

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:02.830
I can't take it! I'm hiding in the well!

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:08.370
I don't wanna die!

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:08.370
Hey! I said, hey!

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:09.410
Huh?

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:12.490
What the hell happened while I was asleep?!

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:15.290
Arrow! You were in the well?!

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:16.950
It's pretty refreshing!

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:23.240
And I promised some Shu guy
I'd stay here, so I can't just run off.

00:19:23.240 --> 00:19:25.910
It's him! He's wrecking the village!

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:27.450
What?!

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:30.200
Jerk! The hell you doing to my village?!

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:33.370
Get him, Arrow! It's not your village, though!

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:38.490
You fool! I inherited
the spirit of the former sheriff!

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:41.200
If I don't protect this place, who will?!

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:42.240
Manifest Armor...

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:44.080
Spirit of the sheriff?

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:46.910
Do you think he meant undies?

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:51.990
Hmm? Looks empty inside,
but I guess I'll haul it back.

00:19:56.450 --> 00:19:58.740
Bring it on, bad guy!

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:02.330
Republic of Rekka   Banned Texts Archive

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:10.660
And now, the most-forbidden text about Rakuho!

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:14.160
Ancient letters, huh?

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:20.080
"One who comes from beyond
sleeps at the edge of land."

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:22.370
Beyond!

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:30.200
Where is this? Am I okay?

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:34.790
Will you register as the startup
system of this Briheight?

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:37.290
Whatever! Just get me outta here!

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:40.080
Startup conviction confirmed.

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:48.120
Are you the Rakuho guy?

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:49.620
What if I am?!

00:20:49.620 --> 00:20:52.120
I'll make you disappear!

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:55.660
That's some strange defense!

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:57.040
You're not half bad!

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:59.870
I've had years of training!

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:05.790
Even so, I won't forgive you
for attacking my village!

00:21:11.990 --> 00:21:14.040
S-So fast!

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:16.200
Blam, blam, blam, blam, blam!

00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:26.660
Huh? I'm not... dead?

00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:28.450
In your face!

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:36.160
"Edger Village is the edge of land.
There, one from beyond sleeps."

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:40.290
That man falling there was destined to happen!

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:45.290
"The encircled world flourished,
and once again, lives tied together.

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:51.240
But when the newcomer reaches self-realization,
the world will be destroyed."

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:52.660
Destroyed?!

00:21:58.870 --> 00:22:05.240
On that fated day, what happened
at Edger put the world in motion.

00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:10.410
Is that which appeared the world's hope

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:12.660
or the herald of destruction?

00:23:47.660 --> 00:23:52.110
Does a Huge Ship Bring Hope?
